WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.185
- I'm a little bit nervous
about exposing this secret

00:00:03.185 --> 00:00:07.268
and I also don't want to,
like, break his heart.

00:00:09.288 --> 00:00:11.497
We're here so I can tell my dad

00:00:11.497 --> 00:00:13.285
a secret that I've been keeping

00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:15.569
for, like, 16 years.

00:00:15.569 --> 00:00:16.402
- I'm nervous.

00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:17.624
I don't know what kind of secret

00:00:17.624 --> 00:00:18.779
she could have since she's four.

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:20.170
- I'm really not that nervous.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.661
I don't think he's going to be that mad.

00:00:21.661 --> 00:00:23.981
Sometimes I makes more
sense not to say something

00:00:23.981 --> 00:00:25.565
if it means you're not
going to get in trouble.

00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:27.333
- I guess I'm excited to
learn about the secret.

00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:29.454
I can't imagine he'd have
anything to hide from me.

00:00:29.454 --> 00:00:30.932
- So, Dad.

00:00:30.932 --> 00:00:31.765
- Nicole.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.098
- What's the one thing that we

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:35.263
used to do together when I was a child?

00:00:35.263 --> 00:00:36.557
Do you remember when you'd ask me,

00:00:36.557 --> 00:00:38.661
"Oh, do you want to play
tennis or golf today?"

00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:39.494
- Yes.

00:00:39.494 --> 00:00:42.252
- My answer 100% of the
time would've been tennis

00:00:42.252 --> 00:00:45.159
because I really, really don't like golf.

00:00:45.159 --> 00:00:47.764
And I never liked playing
it and I just went

00:00:47.764 --> 00:00:50.570
because I wanted to have
something to do with you

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.460
that want me beating you at tennis.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.865
And I also think that
watching golf is really boring

00:00:54.865 --> 00:00:57.054
and I don't understand why you watch it.

00:00:57.054 --> 00:00:59.542
- About two months ago I
got those parking tickets

00:00:59.542 --> 00:01:01.593
and you gave me the money and

00:01:01.593 --> 00:01:03.391
a normal person would've mailed it in.

00:01:03.391 --> 00:01:05.634
And then you called me
one day and were like,

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:06.981
"You never paid the tickets."

00:01:06.981 --> 00:01:07.814
- Yeah.

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:08.824
- "I had to pay the late fee and

00:01:08.824 --> 00:01:11.764
it was about double what the ticket was."

00:01:11.764 --> 00:01:13.698
And I told you that, "It's
just the city's fault."

00:01:13.698 --> 00:01:15.607
I was like, "I paid the tickets,"

00:01:15.607 --> 00:01:17.147
kept the money, and I spent it.

00:01:17.147 --> 00:01:18.847
- But what did you do with the money?

00:01:18.847 --> 00:01:19.691
- 7-11 ...

00:01:19.691 --> 00:01:21.524
- $400 on Slurpees ...

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.578
- You do what you gotta do.

00:01:24.578 --> 00:01:26.457
- Whoa, like a weight's been lifted

00:01:26.457 --> 00:01:27.538
off my shoulders now that you know

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:28.514
and I'm probably not going to watch golf

00:01:28.514 --> 00:01:29.355
with you ever again.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.188
- That's fine.

00:01:30.188 --> 00:01:31.440
- [Interviewer] So, Steven,
how surprised were you?

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.596
- It got to a point
where is became obvious

00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:34.429
that she wasn't that interested in it.

00:01:34.429 --> 00:01:35.944
- It's not that big of a deal.

00:01:35.944 --> 00:01:36.777
- There were late fees.

00:01:36.777 --> 00:01:37.994
You could've just paid the ticket.

00:01:37.994 --> 00:01:39.631
You would put the ticket
on my credit card anyway.

00:01:39.631 --> 00:01:41.454
- I could've put it on the
credit card and kept the money.

00:01:41.454 --> 00:01:42.405
That probably would've been smarter.

00:01:42.405 --> 00:01:44.261
- Why would that be hard for you?

00:01:44.261 --> 00:01:45.094
- I don't know.

00:01:45.094 --> 00:01:45.927
Because you love it.

00:01:45.927 --> 00:01:46.760
- That doesn't break my heart ...

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.484
Actually heartwarming
because at that young age,

00:01:48.484 --> 00:01:49.787
at four years old, you would do something

00:01:49.787 --> 00:01:50.948
that you didn't really like doing

00:01:50.948 --> 00:01:52.379
because you wanted to spend time together.

00:01:52.379 --> 00:01:53.212
- I'm the greatest.

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:54.611
- Now I feel like there's
probably more things

00:01:54.611 --> 00:01:56.593
that you should be telling me.

00:01:56.593 --> 00:01:57.426
- Well ...

00:01:57.426 --> 00:01:58.509
- As opposed to that ...

00:01:58.509 --> 00:01:59.957
- No, that's about as bad as it gets.

00:01:59.957 --> 00:02:01.429
- See, I thought you would be like,

00:02:01.429 --> 00:02:04.584
"Oh, really?" I kind of
expected you to feel cheated

00:02:04.584 --> 00:02:05.928
out of a daughter who liked golf.

00:02:05.928 --> 00:02:06.761
- Well, we can do that another way.

00:02:06.761 --> 00:02:07.594
- Okay. Cool.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.864
- [Interviewer] And how do you feel now

00:02:08.864 --> 00:02:11.025
that you exposed your
supposedly worst secret?

00:02:11.025 --> 00:02:12.264
- I feel about the same.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:13.527
- I still like spending
time with you, though.

00:02:13.527 --> 00:02:15.175
- I mean, you just got another
parking ticket last month.

00:02:15.175 --> 00:02:16.008
Did you pay it?

00:02:16.008 --> 00:02:16.980
- Yeah, I paid it.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.813
- Uh huh ...

00:02:17.813 --> 00:02:18.646
- There are other secrets
that you don't know about.

00:02:18.646 --> 00:02:19.479
- Oh, really?

00:02:19.479 --> 00:02:21.833
- I should actually pay you
when you pay the ticket on time.

00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:23.173
- So if I paid the ticket on time

00:02:23.173 --> 00:02:24.541
you'd give me double the money?

00:02:24.541 --> 00:02:26.936
- I'll give you half of the late fee.

00:02:26.936 --> 00:02:29.071
- This looks like it
worked out better for me

00:02:29.071 --> 00:02:31.321
that I told him the secret.

